      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "**Worker dashboard** — the worker (`apps/worker`) does **not** expose Prometheus metrics yet, so these panels show \"No data\". To activate them, add `@prometheus-io/client` to the worker and expose a `/metrics` endpoint (start a tiny HTTP server on a port just for scraping), then emit:\n\n- `worker_jobs_processed_total{type, status}` — Counter\n- `worker_jobs_failed_total{type}` — Counter\n- `worker_job_duration_seconds{type}` — Histogram (buckets: 0.1, 0.5, 1, 2.5, 5, 10, 30, 60)\n- `worker_active_jobs` — Gauge\n- `worker_queue_depth` — Gauge (poll `LLEN` on your Redis queue)\n\nThen add `{ job_name: worker, static_configs: [{ targets: [\"host.docker.internal:PORT\"] }] }` to `prometheus.yml`.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": { "h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 4 },
      "id": 2,
      "panels": [],
      "title": "Queue & Throughput",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": { "mode": "thresholds" },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "green", "value": null },
              { "color": "yellow", "value": 50 },
              { "color": "red", "value": 100 }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 6, "x": 0, "y": 5 },
      "id": 3,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
